{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"updated\",\n  \"chapter_updates\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch1\",\n      \"updated_plan\": {\n        \"reader_objective\": \"使读者能够准确评估不同实体瘤类型中肠道微生物特征与 ICI 临床结局的观察性关联强度，理解外部干扰因素与纵向动态对关联强度的修饰作用，并清晰区分当前证据的阶梯分布（从强观察性关联到弱干预性概念验证），避免将相关性误读为因果性或普适性生物标志物。\",\n        \"thesis\": \"跨癌种观察性队列证实特定肠道微生物特征（分类学与功能通路）与 ICI 疗效存在显著关联，但缺乏普适性单一标志物；外部药物暴露（抗生素、PPIs）及联合治疗方案构成关键修饰变量，其影响具有明确的时间窗口特异性；基线单次采样难以捕捉治疗诱导的生态重塑，纵向动态变化比静态丰度更能反映真实疗效轨迹；当前证据呈现明显的阶梯状分布，概念验证性干预显示初步希望但异质性大，Phase III RCT 证据完全缺失，且安全性信号受 ICI 方案严格调节。\",\n        \"units\": [\n          {\n            \"argument_relations\": \"共性信号确立微生物-ICI 关联的生物学合理性 → 跨队列异质性统计依据否定普适性单一标志物假设 → 方案特异性修饰效应进一步限制泛化边界。\",\n            \"ordered_development\": \"先展示跨癌种共性信号（高多样性、产 SCFA 菌富集），再指出跨队列荟萃分析揭示的“无通用标志物”现象及癌种特异性反转，最后以 JCOG2007 辅助研究说明方案特异性。\",\n            \"paragraph_briefs\": [\n              {\n                \"development\": \"先列举黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC 等队列中反复出现的阳性信号（如 Akkermansia muciniphila、Bifidobacterium longum、Faecalibacterium prausnitzii 富集及高α多样性），随后指出 mCRPC、HCC 及部分欧洲队列中相同信号失效或反转，说明证据强度呈癌种特异性分布。\",\n                \"finding_conditions\": \"在黑色素瘤、NSCLC 和 RCC 队列中，Akkermansia muciniphila、Bifidobacterium longum 及 Faecalibacterium prausnitzii 富集与更好的 ICI 预后相关（P0096, P0146）；但在 mCRPC 队列中 A. muciniphila 与疗效负相关（P0270），在 HCC 中多界微生物差异显著而真菌差异较小（P0204），在波兰黑色素瘤队列中 F. prausnitzii 与非响应相关（P0545）。\",\n                \"point\": \"展示跨癌种共性信号与癌种特异性分布\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\n                  \"P0096\",\n                  \"P0146\",\n                  \"P0204\",\n                  \"P0270\",\n                  \"P0545\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"development\": \"引用 PERMANOVA 分析结果，证明“队列”本身是解释微生物群落组成变异的最大因素（解释方差远超临床参数），机器学习跨队列泛化能力极差（留一法交叉验证平均 AUC-ROC 仅为 0.59-0.60），确认黑色素瘤 ICI 反应中微生物关联的复杂性和队列依赖性。\",\n                \"finding_conditions\": \"在整合 5 个新测序队列（n=165）和 4 个公开数据集（n=147）后，PERMANOVA 分析显示“队列”因素对微生物群落组成的解释方差是其他任何变量的近十倍；留一法交叉验证的平均 AUC-ROC 仅为 0.59-0.60，仅约 31.4% 的情况超过 0.6（P0478）。\",\n                \"point\": \"解释跨队列异质性与“无通用标志物”的统计依据\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\n                  \"P0478\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"development\": \"对比 NIC（尼莫鲁单抗 + 伊匹木单抗 + 铂类双药）与 PC 组，指出 Fusicatenibacter 和 Butyricicoccus 高丰度仅在 NIC 组中与更好 OS 相关（HR 分别为 0.56 和 0.52），而 Prevotellaceae NK3B31 高丰度在 NIC 组中与更高死亡风险相关（HR=2.33），说明微生物效应方向受具体给药方案严格修饰。\",\n                \"finding_conditions\": \"在 NIC 臂（Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy）vs PC 臂中，Fusicatenibacter 高丰度患者 HR=0.56，Butyricicoccus 高丰度患者 HR=0.52；Prevotellaceae NK3B31 高丰度患者 HR=2.33（P0585）。\",\n                \"point\": \"阐明治疗方案与给药时序的修饰效应\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\n                  \"P0585\",\n                  \"P0015\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ],\n            \"substantive_point\": \"跨癌种观察性队列证实特定肠道微生物特征（分类学与功能通路）与 ICI 疗效存在显著关联，但缺乏普适性单一标志物，证据强度呈癌种特异性分布。\",\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供 NSCLC 背景下跨癌种（黑色素瘤、肾癌）的微生物特征清单，指出特定菌属富集与疗效正相关但存在阈值风险，支撑综述中“跨癌种共性信号与情境依赖性”的论述。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"261e0a3618ae7acf6e831646379929eff88857d5\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0096\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"揭示微生物标志物的肠型特异性（如 E2 肠型中 Collinsella 与响应相关），解释为何单一物种难以成为普适性生物标志物，为“无通用标志物”的统计依据提供群落背景视角。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"4a1e10851c0bf838d11646a65bc0ee57b10b940a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0170\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"证明菌株级签名在联合免疫治疗中具有泛癌种预测力，但在单药队列中失效，直接支撑“治疗方案严格修饰微生物效应方向”及“缺乏普适性单一标志物”的核心论点。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"08a484e3c782bc9552d2df812bad2ec86f231edc\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0015\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供 NSCLC 与黑色素瘤的大样本荟萃分析数据，量化高α多样性及 Akkermansia/Faecalibacterium 富集对 ICI 生存期的正向预后效应，支撑“跨癌种共性信号”的论述。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"82318ae05cff1667b2348961675db67dee4d8360\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0298\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"展示 HCC 多界微生物组特征，揭示细菌/代谢物在持久获益与非获益组间的显著差异而真菌差异较小，用于论证微生物效应具有高度癌种特异性及多界异质性。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"58ddfd822378599d43b877cd0905dfe067a4375f\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0204\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"报道 mCRPC 患者中 A. muciniphila 丰度与 ICI 疗效呈负相关，挑战跨癌种通用正相关假设，并验证 ICI 治疗期间菌群高度稳定，支撑治疗方案史修饰效应及基线决定论。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"74786f8df0c7648840756833a4b4bc49ace34be6\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0270\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供多界微生物组（细菌 + 真菌 + 古菌 + 病毒）整合分析证据，证实高多样性及特定属组合与 ICI 疗效正相关，补充单一细菌视角的局限，支撑“生态网络稳定性促进疗效”的观点。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"a9e58de949ced186b4882146c14b79b306ae9ef5\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0393\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提出“功能趋同”理论框架，解释分类学不一致背后的共享免疫通路（如 SCFA 产生、DC 激活），为跨队列异质性提供机制整合视角，支持向基于功能的生物标志物开发转型。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"9dd62eb058feb9dbd44c28e9c8d004181dd8d19d\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0364\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"展示基因水平微生物丰度结合生物先验知识在预测 ICI 反应中优于传统分类学特征，揭示治疗策略（联合免疫阻断 vs 单药）对微生物信号泛化性的修饰作用，丰富标志物开发的维度。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"bfb5efeaf486304583ce74567d60f84cf138a0ae\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0437\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供波兰队列中饮食模式（高植物/低乳制品）与特定菌群协同影响抗 PD-1 疗效的实证，支撑“微生物标志物具有人群与生活方式依赖性”的分析。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"f31246cd559d1a06b99a32b0ee47bb1ce0265772\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0545\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"系统综述黑色素瘤数据，揭示真菌失调与较差预后的关联，补充单一细菌视角局限，论证多界微生物生态对 ICI 疗效的综合调节作用。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"f9a9ef8d406ee51983cd285f9e60fc41574ae937\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0565\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"基于转移性黑色素瘤宏基因组荟萃分析，确认维生素 B 代谢通路富集与响应正相关，为“功能趋同优于单一分类学标志物”提供跨队列统计支持。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"e533262a6b45c7d00cff83bd889cdc367c85f377\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0511\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"JCOG2007 III 期试验的附属微生物组分析，提供方案特异性（NIC vs PC）微生物 - 疗效关联的高级别证据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"8016df1aa5a8160b7ccd412fa6851a6a508e2731\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0585\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"跨队列黑色素瘤研究，提供“无通用标志物”的具体统计依据及队列间异质性来源分析。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d4c18d58cffce0cab6831c84535e02c608d4db49\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0478\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"transition\": \"既然基线快照与方案特异性已严重限制单一标志物的泛化，必须审视外部药物暴露如何进一步修饰这些关联。\",\n            \"unit_id\": \"U1_跨癌种关联图谱\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"argument_relations\": \"量化暴露效应与时间窗特异性 → 药物诱导的生态重塑机制与宿主背景对比 → 强调校正必要性与残余偏倚风险，确立外部干扰作为核心混杂/修饰变量的地位。\",\n            \"ordered_development\": \"先量化抗生素/PPIs 暴露的效应大小与时间窗特异性，再讨论 PPI 诱导的口腔细菌易位机制及非微生物宿主因素（如肌肉量）的对比，最后强调校正必要性与残余偏倚风险。\",\n            \"paragraph_briefs\": [\n              {\n                \"development\": \"汇总 Meta 分析数据，指出抗生素使用与 OS 恶化（HR=1.61）、PFS 缩短（HR=1.43）及 ORR 降低（RR=0.58）显著相关；亚组分析证实负面关联在 ICI 治疗前后 [-45, 45] 天窗口内最强（β=0.2192, p=0.008），同期 PPIs 暴露亦导致 OS 恶化（HR≈1.31）。\",\n                \"finding_conditions\": \"抗生素暴露与 OS 恶化（HR=1.61, 95% CI 1.44-1.81）、PFS 缩短（HR=1.43, 95% CI 1.27-1.60）及 ORR 降低（RR=0.58, 95% CI 0.51-0.66）显著相关；在 ICI 治疗前后 [-45, 45] 天窗口内使用抗生素，OS 恶化风险最高（β=0.2192, p=0.008）（P0081, P0402, P0236）。\",\n                \"point\": \"量化抗生素/PPIs 暴露的效应量与时间窗特异性\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\n                  \"P0081\",\n                  \"P0402\",\n                  \"P0236\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"development\": \"阐述 PPI 通过改变胃 pH 促进口腔细菌易位至肠道进而缩短 PFS 的机制（P0289），并对比非微生物宿主因素（如低肌肉量）在调整协变量后未显示一致负面预测价值（P0421），说明微生物介导的药物干扰具有独特病理路径。\",\n                \"finding_conditions\": \"PPI 使用者粪便中口腔细菌比例显著升高，且该特征在 PPI 亚组中与更差 PFS 趋势强相关（P0289）；低肌肉量在调整协变量后未降低 PFS 且不增加毒性，作为对比背景说明除菌群外其他宿主因素的预测价值存在异质性（P0421）。\",\n                \"point\": \"讨论药物诱导的生态重塑机制与宿主背景对比\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\n                  \"P0289\",\n                  \"P0421\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"development\": \"指出指示偏倚（Indication Bias）可能导致抗生素负面效应被高估；强调未来研究需标准化暴露定义（种类、剂量、持续时间、指征）并进行多变量校正，否则单纯检测微生物组而不考虑用药史会导致结果不一致。\",\n                \"finding_conditions\": \"观察性研究中的指示偏倚（重症患者更多使用抗生素）可能导致抗生素负面效应被高估；标准化暴露定义与多变量校正是避免结果不一致的必要前提（P0081, P0402）。\",\n                \"point\": \"强调校正必要性与残余偏倚风险\",\n                \"source_handles\": [\n                  \"P0081\",\n                  \"P0402\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ],\n            \"substantive_point\": \"外部药物暴露（抗生素、PPIs）及联合治疗方案构成关键混杂/修饰变量，其影响具有明确的时间窗口特异性和剂量依赖性，需在关联分析中严格校正。\",\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"量化抗酸药（PPIs）使用导致链球菌增加及短 PFS 的关联，并对比化疗预处理对微生物组的持久影响，支撑“外部药物暴露具有明确时间窗特异性与剂量依赖性”的分析任务。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"35f3b135b6c865df8bb304e1f28a8247e55c25fd\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0123\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"汇总抗生素、PPIs 及类固醇暴露对 ICI 预后的负面效应量，特别强调抗生素使用时机（治疗后 vs 治疗前）的差异，为讨论指示偏倚高估负面效应及需标准化校正提供实证对照。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"45ca27020bec6c917c6b71d8b1bad217f5abd0ed\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0157\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"展示 PPI 使用者与非使用者在微生物动态轨迹上的显著差异（如 Streptococcus thermophilus 变化方向相反），说明合并用药可重塑菌群演化路径，需在关联分析中作为关键协变量严格校正。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"0f25b980517704cd7fa782dd9e51d16b77d00249\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0033\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供超 5 万名实体瘤患者的系统综述与荟萃分析数据，量化全身性抗生素暴露导致 PFS 和 OS 显著缩短的效应量，确立抗生素作为负面预后调节因子的流行病学证据等级。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"62379160afa6c14c9a9ae85a0684ccec8ed9c07e\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0236\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"聚焦拉丁美洲 NSCLC 人群，证实抗生素暴露显著降低 OS 但未影响 PFS，提示地域/人群特征可能扰动微生物 - 疗效轴，补充外部干扰效应的群体异质性背景。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"70ba511d3bb0697cd93e53d4880c68ce77471bde\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0266\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"揭示质子泵抑制剂 (PPI) 使用者粪便中口腔细菌比例显著升高，且该特征在 PPI 亚组中与更差 PFS 趋势强相关，阐明合并用药通过重塑肠道生态位构成关键混杂/修饰变量。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"7fe882e8b39d1a041fd2fee47d9321c965f01aa5\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0289\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"针对 HCC 人群的 Meta 分析显示抗生素使用未显著恶化 ICI 疗效 (OS/PFS/ORR)，提出肝硬化基线免疫抑制状态可能缓冲抗生素扰动，为讨论指示偏倚及肿瘤类型特异性校正必要性提供反面对照。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"768ceed11b5509cd8f6c24d07e8fa015646929c0\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0275\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供大样本荟萃分析数据，量化 PPI 使用与 ICI 生存结局恶化的关联，并细化使用时窗（基线/前 60 天 vs 同期）的效应差异，为讨论药物暴露的时间依赖性干扰提供流行病学基准。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"9225e04c4f9620a87d4eb74932067cab87644bf2\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0339\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供妇科肿瘤真实世界数据，明确抗生素使用时长（≥14 天）与 OS 显著缩短的独立关联，区分短期反应指标与长期生存获益的差异，强化用药阈值效应的临床证据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"9cfb62b17064ed5abe1c447f8fa2f46e716b6c0d\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0360\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供肌肉量这一非微生物宿主因素对 ICI 疗效影响的实证数据，显示低肌肉量在肺癌中未降低 PFS 且不增加毒性，作为对比背景说明除菌群外其他宿主因素的预测价值存在异质性。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"b7d5f0bd4b9b2ff5ccb0fca4182d84c2111a7fdf\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0421\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"证实 NSCLC 中抗生素暴露的负面效应高度依赖 PD-L1 表达水平，为“宿主生物标志物状态严格修饰微生物干预效应方向”提供临床分层依据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"e8fb88935a5c5757dc683f56d1ff0c0f356b20ae\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0517\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"系统综述明确 ICI 启动前 30 天内的抗生素暴露是预后恶化的核心风险窗口，同期暴露影响较弱，量化时间窗特异性并提示需区分暴露时机进行校正。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286786239\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0576\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"整合多尺度证据指出抗生素效应在不同实体瘤中存在异质性，警示简单归因于“菌群破坏”，强调需结合肿瘤免疫原性与疾病背景综合评估。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"f381ac20e0012cee8a359a479037e3d12ee6e878\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0548\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Unraveling gut microbiome interferences in cancer immunotherapy: a meta-analysis of diverse drug effects，提供抗生素、PPIs 和益生菌对 ICI 疗效影响的汇总效应量及时间窗特异性数据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"1d2792ae1850f48accaf1c111b2d92b6b2ebc6c0\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0081\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"THE IMPACT OF ANTIBIOTIC THERAPY ON THE EFFECTIVENESS OF IMMUNOTHERAPY: A REVIEW OF CURRENT EVIDENCE，提供抗生素暴露时间依赖性（ICI 前短期暴露负面影响最显著）的叙述性综合证据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"affb01ce6dd2c0ea0909edc814fd8af01596e021\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0402\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"transition\": \"外部干扰虽可量化，但基线单次采样仍难以捕捉治疗诱导的生态重塑，必须转向纵向动态监测。\",\n            \"unit_id\": \"U2_外部干扰与宿主背景\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unit_id_remap\": {}\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to revise the chapter plan for Chapter 1 of a review on gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in solid tumors.\n\n**Task Analysis:**\n1.  **Goal:** Turn supplied whole-plan improvement notes into concrete writer-plan edits for the named chapters (Ch1).\n2.  **Input:**\n    *   `chapter_plan`: Current plan for Ch1 with two modifiable units (`U1_跨癌种关联图谱`, `U2_外部干扰与宿主背景`).\n    *   `source_materials`: A large set of source materials (P0096, P0146, P0585, P0478, P0081, P0402, etc.) with detailed summaries and findings.\n    *   `tool_materials`: Specific Q&A results regarding JCOG2007 trial data (P0585) and Phase III RCT status (failed retrieval, but tool material provides Phase II data).\n    *   `readonly_neighbor_unit_roles`: U3 and U4 (read-only, for context).\n    *   `actual_local_body`: The current drafted text for Ch1 (Units 1.1 and 1.2).\n    *   `review_argument`: A summary of the review's argument.\n    *   `chapter_feedback`: Empty.\n    *   `editorial_feedback_for_chapter`: Empty.\n    *   `planning_revision_mode`: true.\n    *   `autonomous_outline_strengthening`: enabled.\n\n3.  **Constraints:**\n    *   Return JSON only.\n    *   Do not add sources or invent findings.\n    *   Preserve source handles, conditions, and limitations.\n    *   If no change is needed, return `status: no_change`.\n    *   If changes are made, return `status: updated` with `chapter_updates` containing the full updated plan for modifiable units.\n    *   Must use `unit_id_remap` if splitting/merging.\n    *   Do not modify read-only units (U3, U4).\n    *   Ensure the plan aligns with the `actual_local_body` (which seems to already incorporate much of the material) and the `source_materials`.\n    *   Check for factual errors, study-type mismatches, or condition limitations in the current plan vs. the materials.\n\n4.  **Evaluation of Current Plan vs. Materials:**\n    *   **Unit 1 (U1_跨癌种关联图谱):**\n        *   *Thesis:* Cross-cancer observational cohorts confirm associations but lack universal biomarkers; evidence strength is cancer-specific.\n        *   *Paragraph 1 (Common signals vs. Specificity):* Uses P0096, P0146, P0585. The text mentions *Akkermansia*, *Faecalibacterium*, *Bifidobacterium*. Material P0270 (mCRPC) shows *Akkermansia* negative association. P0545 (Polish melanoma) shows *F. prausnitzii* negative. P0204 (HCC) shows multi-kingdom differences. The current plan mentions P0585 for HCC signal reversal, but P0585 is actually NSCLC (JCOG2007). P0204 is HCC. This is a **factual error** in the plan's `finding_conditions` for Paragraph 1. It cites P0585 for HCC signal reversal, but P0585 is NSCLC. P0204 is the HCC study. P0270 is mCRPC. P0545 is Polish Melanoma.\n        *   *Paragraph 2 (Cross-cohort heterogeneity):* Uses P0478. The plan correctly cites PERMANOVA and AUC-ROC stats from P0478.\n        *   *Paragraph 3 (Regimen specificity):* Uses P0585. The plan correctly cites NIC vs PC arms and specific HRs for *Fusicatenibacter*, *Butyricicoccus*, *Prevotellaceae*.\n        *   *Correction Needed:* Fix the citation for HCC signal reversal in Paragraph 1 (should be P0204 or P0275, not P0585). P0585 is NSCLC. Also, P0270 (mCRPC) is a strong example of signal reversal (*Akkermansia* negative).\n    *   **Unit 2 (U2_外部干扰与宿主背景):**\n        *   *Thesis:* External drug exposure (ABX, PPIs) and regimens are key modifiers with time-window specificity.\n        *   *Paragraph 1 (Quantify ABX/PPI):* Uses P0081, P0402. Stats (HR=1.61, etc.) match P0081.\n        *   *Paragraph 2 (Regimen modification):* Uses P0585. This overlaps significantly with U1 Paragraph 3. U1 Para 3 focuses on \"Regimen specificity\" (NIC vs PC). U2 Para 2 focuses on \"Joint regimen modification/reversal\". This is redundant. The current `actual_local_body` puts the JCOG2007 (P0585) regimen specificity discussion in Section 1.1 (under \"Treatment Regimen and Timing Modifier Effects\") AND in Section 1.2 (under \"Joint Regimen Modification\"). This is repetitive.\n        *   *Decision:* The JCOG2007 (P0585) data regarding NIC vs PC arms is fundamentally about *treatment regimen specificity* (Immunotherapy backbone). This fits better in U1 (Association Map/Heterogeneity) as a source of heterogeneity (why biomarkers fail across trials). U2 should focus on *concomitant medications* (ABX, PPIs) and *host background* (like PPI-induced oral bacteria, sarcopenia).\n        *   *Correction Needed:* Move the P0585 regimen specificity point entirely to U1. U2 should focus on ABX/PPI quantification and host factors (PPI mechanism, sarcopenia contrast).\n        *   *Paragraph 3 (Correction/Bias):* Uses P0081, P0402. Discusses indication bias.\n        *   *Refinement:* U2 needs to ensure it doesn't duplicate U1's regimen specificity point. The current plan has P0585 in both U1 Para 3 and U2 Para 2. I should consolidate P0585 in U1. U2 Para 2 should focus on P0585's *safety* data (AEs) or remove it if it's purely efficacy/regimen. Looking at P0585 material: it links *Fusicatenibacter* to OS *and* lower severe AEs. So U2 can keep the *safety* aspect of P0585, but the *efficacy/regimen* aspect belongs in U1.\n        *   *Actually, looking at the `actual_local_body`:* Section 1.2 discusses ABX/PPI quantification, then has a subsection \"Joint Regimen Modification\" (P0585), then \"Correction Necessity\". This structure mirrors the plan. However, since U1 also has a paragraph on \"Regimen Specificity\" (P0585), there is overlap.\n        *   *Optimization:* U1 is about \"Association Map\" (Cancer type, Cohort, Regimen). U2 is about \"External Interference\" (ABX, PPI, Host). P0585 is a Phase III trial ancillary study. It shows regimen specificity (NIC vs PC). This is a source of heterogeneity for biomarkers (U1). It also shows safety association (U2?). The prompt says U2 is \"External Interference & Host Background\". ABX/PPI are external interference. Regimen (NIC vs PC) is part of the ICI treatment itself, not exactly \"external interference\" like ABX. So P0585 efficacy data fits U1 better. P0585 safety data could fit U2 or Ch6. Given Ch6 is Toxicity, maybe P0585 safety belongs there? But Ch1 scope includes \"clinical association evidence\".\n        *   *Better Split:* U1: Biomarker associations (Cancer type, Cohort, Regimen). U2: Confounders (ABX, PPI, Host factors like sarcopenia).\n        *   *Action:* Remove P0585 efficacy/regimen specificity from U2 Para 2. Keep it in U1 Para 3. U2 Para 2 should focus on PPI mechanism (oral bacteria translocation P0289) or Host factors (Sarcopenia P0421) to distinguish from ABX. Or simply strengthen the ABX/PPI time-window discussion.\n        *   *Wait, looking at U2 Para 2 in current plan:* \"Compare NIC vs PC...\". This is identical to U1 Para 3. This is definitely redundant. I will remove U2 Para 2's focus on P0585 efficacy and replace it with P0289 (PPI/Oral bacteria mechanism) or P0421 (Sarcopenia contrast) to flesh out \"Host Background\". The unit title is \"External Interference & Host Background\".\n        *   *Revised U2 Structure:*\n            1.  Quantify ABX/PPI effects (P0081, P0402, P0236).\n            2.  Mechanism/Host Context: PPI -> Oral bacteria (P0289) OR Host factors like Sarcopenia (P0421) as a contrast/non-microbiome factor.\n            3.  Bias/Correction (P0081, P0402).\n\n    *   **Source Handle Check:**\n        *   U1 Para 1: P0096, P0146, P0585 (for HCC? No, P0585 is NSCLC). Need to fix citation. Use P0204 (HCC), P0270 (mCRPC), P0545 (Polish Melanoma).\n        *   U1 Para 2: P0478. Correct.\n        *   U1 Para 3: P0585, P0015. Correct.\n        *   U2 Para 1: P0081, P0402, P0236. Correct.\n        *   U2 Para 2: Currently P0585 (Duplicate). Change to P0289 (PPI/Oral bacteria) or P0421 (Sarcopenia). Let's use P0289 to explain *how* PPI works (mechanism/context) and P0421 to show non-microbiome host factors.\n        *   U2 Para 3: P0081, P0402. Correct.\n\n    *   **Material Consistency:**\n        *   P0585 is JCOG2007 (NSCLC). The plan currently says \"HCC... (P0585)\". This is a factual error.\n        *   P0204 is HCC multi-kingdom.\n        *   P0270 is mCRPC (Akkermansia negative).\n        *   P0545 is Polish Melanoma (F. prausnitzii negative).\n        *   P0081 is Meta-analysis on ABX/PPI.\n        *   P0289 is SCRUM-Japan (PPI/Oral bacteria).\n        *   P0421 is Sarcopenia.\n\n    *   **Plan Update Strategy:**\n        1.  Fix U1 Para 1 `finding_conditions` and `source_handles` to correctly attribute HCC (P0204) and mCRPC (P0270) signal reversals, removing P0585 from this specific point.\n        2.  Fix U2 Para 2 to remove redundancy with U1 Para 3. Replace P0585 efficacy discussion with P0289 (PPI mechanism) and P0421 (Host factor contrast).\n        3.  Ensure `source_handles` in `paragraph_briefs` match the `supporting_studies`.\n        4.  Keep `unit_id`s stable.\n\n5.  **Drafting the Updates:**\n    *   **U1:**\n        *   Para 1: Update finding_conditions to cite P0204 for HCC, P0270 for mCRPC, P0545 for Polish Melanoma. Keep P0096/P0146 for positive signals.\n        *   Para 2: Keep P0478.\n        *   Para 3: Keep P0585 (NIC vs PC) and P0015 (Strain/Regimen).\n    *   **U2:**\n        *   Para 1: Keep P0081, P0402, add P0236 (large meta-analysis).\n        *   Para 2: Change to P0289 (PPI -> Oral bacteria -> PFS) and P0421 (Sarcopenia non-microbiome contrast). Remove P0585.\n        *   Para 3: Keep P0081, P0402.\n\n6.  **Review against Constraints:**\n    *   JSON only.\n    *   Complete updated_plan for modifiable units.\n    *   Preserve source handles (but correct misattributions).\n    *   No new evidence (using existing source_materials).\n    *   Status: updated.\n\n7.  **Final Check:**\n    *   Did I fix the P0585 HCC error? Yes.\n    *   Did I remove U1/U2 redundancy on P0585? Yes (U1 keeps regimen efficacy, U2 keeps ABX/PPI/Host).\n    *   Are source handles valid? Yes.\n    *   Is the structure logical? Yes.\n\n    *Self-Correction on U2 Para 2:* The unit title is \"External Interference & Host Background\". P0289 (PPI effect) fits \"External Interference\". P0421 (Sarcopenia) fits \"Host Background\". This is a good replacement for the duplicate P0585 regimen point.\n\n    *Self-Correction on U1 Para 1:* The current plan says \"HCC... (P0585)\". P0585 is NSCLC. P0204 is HCC. P0270 is mCRPC. I will update the `finding_conditions` text and `source_handles`.\n\n    *Unit IDs:* U1_跨癌种关联图谱，U2_外部干扰与宿主背景。Keep these.\n\n    *Supporting Studies:* Need to ensure the `supporting_studies` list in each unit reflects the paragraphs.\n    *   U1 Supporting: P0096, P0146, P0015, P0298, P0204, P0289, P0270, P0393, P0364, P0437, P0545, P0565, P0511, P0585. (Ensure P0585 is here for Para 3, P0204/P0270/P0545 for Para 1).\n    *   U2 Supporting: P0081, P0123, P0157, P0033, P0236, P0266, P0289, P0275, P0339, P0360, P0421, P0517, P0576, P0548. (Ensure P0289/P0421 are highlighted for Para 2).\n\n    *Wait, one detail:* The `actual_local_body` already has the text. I am planning the *chapter_plan* to match the *body* and *materials*. The body has Section 1.1 (U1) and 1.2 (U2).\n    *   Body 1.1 Para 3 discusses JCOG2007 (P0585).\n    *   Body 1.2 Para 2 discusses JCOG2007 (P0585) *again*.\n    *   My plan update should reflect the *intended* structure. Since I am fixing the plan, I should ensure the plan *directs* the writer to avoid redundancy in future revisions or aligns with the current body if the body is considered the \"truth\". However, the instruction says \"Turn the supplied whole-plan improvement notes into concrete writer-plan edits\". The `actual_local_body` is provided as context (\"input_integrity\"). If the body has redundancy, the plan should ideally guide towards a better structure if I am allowed to edit the plan. The instruction says \"Inspect the supplied plan and evidence, then make only material-backed outline improvements worth carrying downstream.\" Removing redundancy is a valid improvement.\n    *   So I will remove P0585 efficacy from U2 Para 2 in the plan, even if the body currently has it, to guide future coherence. Or, I can note that U2 Para 2 should focus on *safety* if keeping P0585. But P0289/P0421 is better for \"Host Background\". I will switch U2 Para 2 to P0289/P0421.\n\n    *Let's check the source_materials for P0289 and P0421.*\n    *   P0289: SCRUM-Japan. PPI -> Oral bacteria -> PFS.\n    *   P0421: Sarcopenia. Low muscle mass not associated with worse PFS/OS in ICI (contrast to microbiome).\n    *   These are available in `source_materials`.\n\n    *Let's check P0204, P0270, P0545 for U1 Para 1.*\n    *   P0204: HCC multi-kingdom.\n    *   P0270: mCRPC (Akkermansia negative).\n    *   P0545: Polish Melanoma (F. prausnitzii negative).\n    *   These are available.\n\n    *Let's check P0585 for U1 Para 3.*\n    *   P0585: JCOG2007 NSCLC. NIC vs PC.\n    *   Available.\n\n    *Plan Update:*\n    *   U1 Para 1: Update `finding_conditions` to correctly cite P0204 (HCC), P0270 (mCRPC), P0545 (Polish). Remove P0585 from this paragraph's handles.\n    *   U2 Para 2: Update `point` to \"Elucidate PPI mechanism (oral bacteria) and contrast non-microbiome host factors\". Update `finding_conditions` to P0289 and P0421. Remove P0585.\n\n    *Wait, one more check:* The `actual_local_body` Section 1.2 *does* have a subsection \"Joint Regimen Modification\" using P0585. If I change the plan, I am suggesting a structural change. Is that allowed? \"make only material-backed outline improvements worth carrying downstream.\" Yes, removing redundancy is an improvement.\n    *   However, I must ensure I don't delete content that is already written if I can't change the body. But I am returning a *plan*. The writer will use the plan to write/revise. If the plan says \"Don't put P0585 here\", the writer should move it.\n    *   Actually, looking at U1 Para 3, it covers \"Regimen Specificity\". U2 Para 2 covers \"Joint Regimen Modification\". These are the same thing. I will consolidate in U1. U2 will focus on ABX/PPI/Host.\n\n    *Final Plan Structure:*\n    *   U1: Associations (Cancer type, Cohort, Regimen).\n    *   U2: Confounders (ABX, PPI, Host).\n\n    *Let's construct the JSON.*","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":132267,"completion_tokens":10230,"total_tokens":142497,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4585,"text_tokens":10230},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":132267}},"created":1791261888,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-c8a44c2b-b8df-9bbd-994b-00e268de8076"}